#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:3 c74e3bb4ddff4e4ebce63901b129712b
msgid "Issue tracking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:6 31d07e60d81d4b4e9d0b3917c032059f
msgid ""
"We use `GitHub Issues <https://docs.github.com/en/issues>`__ as our `issue "
"tracking system <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Issue_tracking_system>`__. "
"All issues pertaining to the Qubes OS Project (including auxiliary "
"infrastructure such as this website) are tracked in `qubes-issues <https://"
"github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:9 c27fb2cd931843319749249e7e63c991
msgid "How to open a new issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:12 03f800ded0614811bea783ff83d58348
msgid "First, let’s make sure the issue tracker is the right place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:15 ffc12278bd9e49d6a5b1d6fd3a8aa2df
msgid "I need help, have a question, or want to discuss something."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:18 44e5ff84ed2740968befef0fd485f398
msgid ""
"We’re happy to help, answer questions, and have discussions, but the issue "
"tracker is not the right place for these activities. Instead, please see :"
"doc:`Help, Support, Mailing Lists, and Forum </introduction/support>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:21 3a6dc70656874e079458034fa9fc40b5
msgid "I see something that should be changed in the documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:24 13b52efb307a463e9df01e1baaec9897
msgid ""
"We encourage you to submit the change yourself! Please see the :doc:`how to "
"edit the documentation </developer/general/how-to-edit-the-rst-"
"documentation>` for instructions on how to do so. If it’s something you "
"can’t do yourself, please proceed to open an issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:27 ec09b5857d23411f9d5433d20c68d16c
msgid "I would like to report a security vulnerability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:30 06268a84bcf44276a4bdf1de3255c3b1
msgid ""
"Thank you! If the vulnerability is confidential, please do not report it in "
"our public issue tracker. Instead, please see :ref:`Reporting Security "
"Issues in Qubes OS <project-security/security:reporting security issues in "
"qubes os>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:33 c3dbb230f8c9407bba3e53a0f51ec848
msgid "I still want to open an issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:36 aa1b446f3bf04f74816d1ce85961e6c9
msgid ""
"Great! Thank you for taking the time and effort to help improve Qubes! To "
"ensure the process is efficient and productive for everyone involved, please "
"follow these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:38 02d5117c7e61470c9930c64a2618bae1
msgid ""
"Carefully read our issue tracking :ref:`introduction/issue-tracking:"
"guidelines`. If your issue would violate any of the guidelines, **stop**. "
"Please do not submit it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:40 51aa8d6e3ece400db093bc945980d88b
msgid ""
":ref:`Search through the existing issues <introduction/issue-tracking:search "
"tips>`, both open and closed, to see if your issue already exists. If it "
"does, **stop**. :ref:`Do not open a duplicate. <introduction/issue-tracking:"
"new issues should not be duplicates of existing issues>` Instead, comment on "
"the existing issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:42 3aad3be8814340fdb880c56127a978c8
msgid ""
"Go `here <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues/new/choose>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:44 4af9623d464b41ffb2bd72f9e236df8b
msgid ""
"Select the :ref:`type <introduction/issue-tracking:types>` of issue you want "
"to open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:46 793b1c1c9b6e4fe28fdb3921060aca81
msgid "Enter a descriptive title."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:48 d7bbf6cc29a348ee82f769eb79458a3f
msgid ""
"Do not delete the provided issue template. Fill out every applicable section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:50 b9ce34eb5779493f87a0b187274393cc
msgid ""
"Please note that AIs often `hallucinate <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Hallucination_(artificial_intelligence)>`__ about Qubes OS. If you're using "
"an AI to assist you, please check its conclusions against the `official "
"documentation <https://doc.qubes-os.org/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:52 02b22848fc864bc286256ee56542217e
msgid ""
"Make sure to mention any relevant documentation and other issues you’ve "
"already seen. We don’t know what you’ve seen unless you tell us. If you "
"don’t list it, we’ll assume you haven’t seen it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:54 93030cbfbc404961a853bb5615024c36
msgid ""
"If any sections of the issue template are *truly* not applicable, you may "
"remove them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:56 904e62b855f543b5b73d6f65a8d8f9b2
msgid "Submit your issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:58 5cb110525c514090b138ad53f3632761
msgid ""
"Respond to any questions the official team asks. For example, you may be "
"asked to provide specific logs or other additional information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:62 172597cc33894cdd8b69c45cca06c82c
msgid ""
"Eventually, your issue may be closed. See :ref:`how issues get closed "
"<introduction/issue-tracking:how issues get closed>` for details about when, "
"why, and how this occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:65 3e0744b869eb40f0a94c2e493fd3eb53
msgid "How issues are organized"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:68 605080c6632c4bb9ba90179bbf0c68b2
msgid ""
"Issues can have several different properties and be organized in various "
"ways. This section explains how we use labels, issue types, projects, and "
"other features of GitHub’s issue tracking system in order to keep `qubes-"
"issues <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues>`__ organized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:71 9560accce05c48d5a31c6ceead0f5768
msgid "Labels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:74 9b8329889fbd4db9b4c61dd136c60bcf
msgid ""
"When an issue is first created, it will receive the ``P: default`` (i.e., "
"default priority) `label <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/labels>`__ "
"automatically. After an issue has been created, only Qubes team members have "
"permission to modify labels. Many labels have descriptions on them that can "
"be viewed by hovering over them or on the `list of labels <https://github."
"com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/labels>`__. Let’s go over some of the most "
"important ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:77 7060ab8a901643bda7351fced374ec65
msgid "Priority"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:80 7d6f9f19ccc6430499bc6cebbe7b79c5
msgid ""
"There are several issue **priority** levels ranging from ``P: minor`` to "
"``P: blocker`` (see `here <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/labels?"
"q=P%3A>`__ for the full list). Every open issue should have exactly one "
"priority. An open issue should not have more than one priority, and it "
"should not lack a priority entirely. See :ref:`here <developer/releases/"
"version-scheme:bug priorities>` for details about how the developers use "
"these priorities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:83 c0b90c84261b4d4ebcc7281fddcd3363
msgid "Component"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:86 ef82aa0a822140abbee79355969120a2
msgid ""
"There are many **component** labels, each beginning with ``C:`` (see `here "
"<https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/labels?q=C%3A>`__ for the full "
"list). Every open issue should have at least one component. An open issue "
"may have more than one component, but it should not lack a component "
"entirely. When no other component applies, use ``C: other``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:89 7ad419f44ea845ccb811bc3580a3c098
msgid "Affected release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:92 c3143660d4f04534b955b39a175b5e54
msgid ""
"A label of the form ``affects-<RELEASE_NUMBER>`` indicates that an issue "
"affects the corresponding Qubes OS release. An issue can have more than one "
"of these labels if it affects multiple releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:95 f653027507d544bfa86a6f5c3b23b0fb
msgid "Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:98 1d1a6273bf744d5cbacc458d78d145a6
msgid ""
"There are three issue `types <https://docs.github.com/en/issues/tracking-"
"your-work-with-issues/configuring-issues/managing-issue-types-in-an-"
"organization>`__: Bug, Feature, and Task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:100
#: 03ea54cc418f498e807e4ed894a6b184
msgid "**Bug** — An unexpected problem or behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:102
#: f3fd7bc4f79245b7adb45cae20d1996f
msgid "**Feature** — A request, idea, or new functionality"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:104
#: 27ce09aab543452a8a4e58e937d419cf
msgid "**Task** — A specific piece of work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:108
#: 81ba790629054613aad316d7da2d7eef
msgid ""
"Every open issue should have exactly one type. **Bug** reports are for "
"problems in things that already exist. If something doesn’t exist yet, but "
"you think it ought to exist, then that issue should instead be a **Feature** "
"request. If something already exists, but you think it could be improved in "
"some way, that also qualifies as a **Feature** request. The **Task** type is "
"for issues that are actionable but that fall under neither the **Bug** nor "
"**Feature** types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:111
#: 1a668b3222ba4d27b829ae91826eb6bd
msgid "Projects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:114
#: c8a3e1ba64484c8994c4ab26d15e08dd
msgid ""
"According to GitHub, a `project <https://docs.github.com/en/issues/planning-"
"and-tracking-with-projects/learning-about-projects/about-projects>`__ is “an "
"adaptable spreadsheet, task-board, and road map that integrates with your "
"issues and pull requests on GitHub to help you plan and track your work "
"effectively.” The issue tracker has several `projects <https://github.com/"
"QubesOS/qubes-issues/projects>`__. Github projects allows more detailed "
"issue states, and also attaching more metadata to issues. They also allow "
"more focused view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:116
#: 01bdd8e515e54acab4e9c4b031bb29a0
msgid ""
"There is a special project in Qubes OS project: the `Current team tasks "
"project <https://github.com/orgs/QubesOS/projects/19/views/1>`__ which "
"represents current work of the core team. Issues in this project’s "
"**backlog** section are not yet ready for work - they might be waiting for "
"clarifications, blockers, decisions on priorities etc. Issues that are "
"**ready** can be picked up by any team member. There should not be too many "
"issues in **ready** column to decrease confusion and decision paralysis - "
"good number is around 20. The **in review** state means that the developer "
"is finished with the work (the completion state has been reached) - if "
"something has to be postponed or abandoned, a justification should be posted "
"in issue discussion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:119
#: ed1cbe22137143b89b1d3b165aa19608
msgid "Meta-issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:122
#: 8ef639ba29fd4c4496c31f5452c783d1
msgid ""
"A meta-issue is an issue that serves primarily to collect and organize a "
"group of other issues. This group of other issues typically exists in a "
"hierarchy of `sub-issues <https://docs.github.com/en/issues/tracking-your-"
"work-with-issues/using-issues/adding-sub-issues>`__, usually with the meta-"
"issue at the top. (For example, we use meta-issues when we need a way to "
"track work on specific features. We cannot use :ref:`introduction/issue-"
"tracking:projects` for this, because we already use a project for tracking "
"the work of the Qubes team as a whole, and projects cannot contain "
"milestones or other projects.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:124
#: 909ad3978ae744c4afe6b8049f68985e
msgid ""
"Meta-issues should have informative descriptions, not just lists of issues. "
"In particular, each meta-issue should explain its goal, what is in scope, "
"and what the relevant categories and priorities are."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:126
#: e0c5b6e390dd43b397e16694832df6a4
msgid ""
"In addition, meta-issues should have clear, concrete, and actionable "
"criteria for when they will be closed. Meta-issues should never be “open-"
"ended” or expected to stay open indefinitely. If this ever becomes unclear, "
"the meta-issue should be closed until it becomes clear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:129
#: 600d6dd4da73488f96dbc951249266a5
msgid "Search tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:132
#: 905f74137be0488f9703a7b231900d25
msgid ""
"`Search both open and closed issues. <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-"
"issues/issues?utf8=%E2%9C%93&q=is%3Aissue>`__ For example, you may be "
"experiencing a bug that was just fixed, in which case the report for that "
"bug is probably closed. In this case, it would be useful to view `all bug "
"reports, both open and closed, with the most recently updated sorted to the "
"top <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues?q=sort%3Aupdated-"
"desc%20type%3ABug>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:134
#: b909a80e7b534ee59c9978f9fd6ab529
msgid ""
"`Search with labels. <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/labels>`__ For "
"example, you can search issues by priority (`blocker <https://github.com/"
"QubesOS/qubes-issues/labels/P%3A%20blocker>`__, `critical <https://github."
"com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/labels/P%3A%20critical>`__, `major <https://github."
"com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/labels/P%3A%20major>`__, etc.) and by component "
"(`core <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues?"
"q=is%3Aopen%20is%3Aissue%20label%3A%22C%3A%20core%22>`__, `manager/widget "
"<https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues?"
"utf8=%E2%9C%93&q=is%3Aopen%20is%3Aissue%20label%3A%22C%3A%20manager%2Fwidget%22+>`__, "
"`Xen <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues?"
"q=is%3Aopen%20is%3Aissue%20label%3A%22C%3A%20Xen%22>`__, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:136
#: d4fd1ade72f146868df40d445b82e780
msgid ""
"Search by closure reason: `reason:completed <https://github.com/QubesOS/"
"qubes-issues/issues?q=reason%3Acompleted>`__ and `reason:\"not planned\" "
"<https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues?"
"q=reason%3A%22not%20planned%22>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:138
#: 53c7f17d67784f1ca616b668c11db6a0
msgid ""
"`Search by project <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/projects>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:143
#: ab0648483f584f2fb7748a1dcc218d82
msgid "Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:147
#: 87ac80c8ac8748ceb34ba8ad1534912a
msgid "The issue tracker is not a discussion forum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:150
#: 619a331377384bfe8d0dc35b0d6c3cbd
msgid ""
"The issue tracker is a tool to help the developers be more productive and "
"efficient in their work. It is not a place for discussion. If you wish to "
"discuss something in the issue tracker, please do so on the forum or mailing "
"lists (see :doc:`Help, Support, Mailing Lists, and Forum </introduction/"
"support>`). You can simply link to the relevant issue in your discussion "
"post."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:152
#: 6b5f6412dd0d480eb3b2e8d32c10fe60
msgid ""
"This guideline is important for keeping issues focused on *actionable "
"information*, which helps the developers to stay focused on their work. When "
"developers come back to an issue to work on it, we do not want them to have "
"to sift through a large number of unnecessary comments before they can get "
"started. In many cases, an issue that gets “too big” essentially becomes "
"more trouble than it’s worth, and no developer will touch it (also see :ref:"
"`introduction/issue-tracking:every issue must be about a single, actionable "
"thing`). In these cases, we sometimes have to close the issue and open a new "
"one. This is a waste of energy for everyone involved, so we ask that "
"everyone help to avoid repeating this pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:155
#: 42697ea15d5c4068a89bd4d05c1c20b1
msgid "Do not submit questions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:158
#: 56d7b1f2bfb147e1b74841d805530ebe
msgid ""
"`qubes-issues <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues>`__ is not the "
"place to ask questions. This includes, but is not limited to, "
"troubleshooting questions and questions about how to do things with Qubes. "
"Instead, see :doc:`Help, Support, Mailing Lists, and Forum </introduction/"
"support>` for appropriate places to ask questions. By contrast, `qubes-"
"issues <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues>`__ is meant for "
"tracking more general bugs, enhancements, and tasks that affect a broad "
"range of Qubes users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:161
#: 50f55041ec2349219cddcf02736b5431
msgid "Use the issue template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:164
#: 1a557ba0526244468157021a934d39ee
msgid ""
"When you open a new issue, an issue template is provided for you. Please use "
"it. Do not delete it. The issue template is carefully designed to elicit "
"important information. Without this information, the issue is likely to be "
"incomplete. (If certain sections are not applicable, you may remove them, "
"but please do so only sparingly and only if they are *truly* not applicable.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:166
#: 8b9a13d3fc0b42989ebb3e81bb9f5256
msgid ""
"It is also important to note the placement and content of the HTML comments "
"in the issue template. These help us to have issues with a consistent format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:169
#: 85bb7af44f5f490f93b48c1ef036bb82
msgid "Every issue must be about a single, actionable thing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:172
#: 8d64e87274c543beb796562e2fb12864
msgid ""
"If your issue is not actionable, please see :doc:`Help, Support, Mailing "
"Lists, and Forum </introduction/support>` for the appropriate place to post "
"it. If your issue would be about more than one thing, file them as separate "
"issues instead. This means we should generally not try to use a single issue "
"as a “meta” or “epic” issue that exists only to group, contain, or track "
"other issues. Instead, when there is a need to group multiple related issues "
"together, use `projects <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/"
"projects>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:174
#: 4e4c58463b914bf18b1e2f13396127c1
msgid ""
"This guideline is extremely important for making the issue tracker a useful "
"tool for the developers. When an issue is too big and composite, it becomes "
"intractable and drastically increases the likelihood that nothing will get "
"done. Such issues also tend to encourage an excessive amount of general "
"discussion that is simply not appropriate for a technical issue tracker "
"(see :ref:`introduction/issue-tracking:the issue tracker is not a discussion "
"forum`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:177
#: 05ffe3676361448cb2cf967409d95b63
msgid "Every issue must be of a single type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:180
#: b9205fbba635484a85a467e86cf48db9
msgid ""
"Every issue must be exactly one of the following types: a bug report "
"(``bug``), a feature or improvement request (``enhancement``), or a task "
"(``task``). Do not file multi-typed issues. Instead, file multiple issues of "
"distinct types. The Qubes team will classify your issue according to its "
"type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:183
#: e596cefc3484422782e95c40dcfd6131
msgid "New issues should not be duplicates of existing issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:186
#: 2be2a6ac550b4f0784a5177968c2bf5d
msgid ""
"Before you submit an issue, check to see whether it has already been "
"reported. Search through the existing issues – both open and closed – by "
"typing your key words in the **Filters** box. If you find an issue that "
"seems to be similar to yours, read through it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:188
#: d839c7b84a9f4cf58bbae650d1e84194
msgid ""
"For bug reports, if you find an issue that is the same as or subsumes yours, "
"leave a comment on the existing bug report issue rather than opening a new "
"one, even if the existing bug report is closed (unless the existing issue "
"was fixed a long time ago, in which case it's likely a different bug with "
"similar symptoms). If a bug report affects more than one supported Qubes "
"release, we usually keep only one bug report for all currently-supported "
"releases. If a bug report was closed due to all affected releases reaching "
"end of life at the time, and you're experiencing the same bug on a currently-"
"supported release, please leave a comment saying so. We will reopen the "
"issue and update it to reflect the fact that it has been reported to affect "
"the currently-supported release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:190
#: 01c674c9221d43e2a7fe31e460b88b18
msgid ""
"For feature requests, if the initial implementation was incomplete or "
"unsuccessful, then please leave a comment on the existing feature request "
"issue, and we will reopen it. However, if the initial implementation of the "
"feature was successful, and you are reporting a problem with the feature "
"that arose later, then please open a separate bug report (if one doesn't "
"already exist for that bug) instead of commenting on the old feature "
"request, as we generally prefer not to reopen old feature requests the "
"initial implementation of which was successfully completed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:192
#: e66d105177474e459903af4fcf5353a0
msgid ""
"Whenever you leave a comment on an issue, the Qubes team will see your "
"comment and take appropriate action on that issue. For example, you can "
"leave a comment with additional information to help the maintainer debug a "
"problem. Adding a comment will subscribe you to email notifications, which "
"can be helpful in getting important updates regarding the issue. If you "
"don’t have anything to add but still want to receive email updates, you can "
"click the “Subscribe” button on the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:196
#: ed84b4f134544675bfad3a526bacb80c
msgid "New issues should include all relevant information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:199
#: cbe55024b231415fa2b3e937813c79de
msgid ""
"When you file a new issue, you should be sure to include the version of "
"Qubes you’re using, as well as versions of related software packages (:doc:"
"`how to copy information out of dom0 </user/how-to-guides/how-to-copy-from-"
"dom0>`). If your issue is related to hardware, provide as many details as "
"possible about the hardware. A great way to do this is by :ref:`generating "
"and submitting a Hardware Compatibility List (HCL) report <user/hardware/how-"
"to-use-the-hcl:generating and submitting new reports>`, then linking to it "
"in your issue. You may also need to use command-line tools such as "
"``lspci``. If you’re reporting a bug in a package that is in a :doc:`testing "
"</user/downloading-installing-upgrading/testing>` repository, please "
"reference the appropriate issue in the `updates-status <https://github.com/"
"QubesOS/updates-status/issues>`__ repository. Project maintainers really "
"appreciate thorough explanations. It usually helps them address the problem "
"more quickly, so everyone wins!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:202
#: 134f06e614a74aa4900f71f85349f601
msgid "There are no guarantees that your issue will be addressed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:205
#: 6d3e8439b359423ea6b9e6d38d45f958
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that `qubes-issues <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/"
"issues>`__ is an issue tracker, not a support system. Creating a new issue "
"is simply a way for you to submit an item for the Qubes team’s "
"consideration. It is up to the Qubes team to decide whether or how to "
"address your issue, which may include closing the issue without taking any "
"action on it. Even if your issue is kept open, however, you should not "
"expect it to be addressed within any particular time frame, or at all. At "
"the time of this writing, there are well over one thousand open issues in "
"`qubes-issues <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues>`__. The Qubes "
"team has its own roadmap and priorities, which will govern the manner and "
"order in which open issues are addressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:208
#: 675259a39b54481e9be65b2a37fabca0
msgid "Issues and comments must be written in English"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:211
#: aff362ef5d2e49aca0b0600ea427a24e
msgid ""
"If English is not your native language, you may post a machine translation. "
"If you wish, you may also include the original non-English text in a :ref:"
"`collapsible section <introduction/issue-tracking:use collapsible sections "
"for long, nonessential content>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:214
#: 54d6c3aa8efc4acdbecd5476d4ba4582
msgid "Developers may ask you for logs or other data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:217
#: f1f60d21f9334ba28f7272a27ced9dfb
msgid ""
"In some cases, Qubes developers who are working on an issue may request logs "
"or other data from you. Qubes OS *never* sends such data automatically, and "
"you are *never* required to provide it. However, without access to the logs, "
"it may not be possible for the developers to diagnose and fix the bug you're "
"experiencing. *If you wish to do so*, you *may* provide such data, for "
"example, by posting it in a comment on the relevant issue. This is fine when "
"the data is not sensitive. However, since issues are publicly visible, you "
"should not post any sensitive data there. If the data that a Qubes developer "
"wants from you is sensitive in any way, and if you're comfortable sharing it "
"with the Qubes team, then we strongly recommend using encryption. The most "
"common method is to send it in a PGP-encrypted email, then add a comment on "
"the issue stating that you've sent the email. You can find the Qubes "
"developers' email PGP keys on the `Team <https://www.qubes-os.org/team/>`__ "
"page and in the :doc:`Qubes security pack (qubes-secpack) </project-security/"
"security-pack>`. Share the information inline or as a file attachment. "
"Please do not just send a link to a pastebin or file-hosting service, as "
"there's a risk that it will expire before the issue is resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:219
#: 2df048258ad7461d8d142df8b35543c8
msgid ""
"In some cases, one Qubes developer may start working on an issue, then "
"another one may take over some time later. If you send logs or other data to "
"the first developer, the second developer will also need access to that "
"data. Therefore, by sharing data with a member of the Qubes team, you "
"thereby grant them permission to share that data with the rest of the Qubes "
"team. Please do not share any data with a member of the Qubes team unless "
"you are comfortable with the entire team having access to that data. (This "
"is also why it's important for you to leave a comment on the issue stating "
"that you emailed data to a specific developer, as it allows other developers "
"to know that data was sent and to whom.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:221
#: ad33fc8e87af44b48bfacc0f63c5f79d
msgid ""
"Please **do not** send unsolicited communications to developers or attempt "
"to contact them directly for help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:224
#: ffaa93fb819d4a31bf4e9a07d9410ef9
msgid "Use collapsible sections for long, nonessential content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:227
#: 62ac57bb8278447aa2cdda8440303b45
msgid "On GitHub, create collapsible sections in Markdown like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:240
#: bc3eb374d8a14085b6f5cf1fb6d96bfa
msgid ""
"**Tip:** Use the “Preview” tab to make sure it renders correctly before "
"posting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:243
#: 7fc49678c5c945ed95d75b16f316d0e0
msgid "How issues get closed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:246
#: 89f67d7210314fbfb2255a5032e836f4
msgid ""
"If the Qubes developers make a code change that resolves an issue, then the "
"issue will typically be `closed from the relevant commit or merged pull "
"request (PR) <https://docs.github.com/en/issues/tracking-your-work-with-"
"issues/creating-issues/linking-a-pull-request-to-an-issue>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:249
#: 61ccaa0488354c06943ea3d56cfc020c
msgid "Bug reports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:252
#: 41656c1a46884452aa6d10145d6f8fe3
msgid ""
"In the case of bugs, the package containing the change will move to the "
"appropriate :doc:`testing </user/downloading-installing-upgrading/testing>` "
"repository, then to the appropriate stable repository. If you so choose, you "
"can test the fix while it’s in the :doc:`testing </user/downloading-"
"installing-upgrading/testing>` repository, or you can wait for it to land in "
"the stable repository. If, after testing the fix, you find that it does not "
"really fix the reported bug, please leave a comment on the issue explaining "
"the situation. When you do, we will receive a notification and respond on "
"the issue or reopen it (or both). Please **do not** create a duplicate issue "
"or attempt to contact the developers individually about a problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:255
#: 52fd0def5acb4cacb4eae2c5e1cf4af0
msgid "Resolution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:258
#: e14b70b2340041a0812d467be7c91c0f
msgid ""
"In GitHub, an issue can be `closed as either \"completed\" or \"not "
"planned\" <https://github.blog/changelog/2022-03-10-the-new-github-issues-"
"march-10th-update/#%F0%9F%95%B5%F0%9F%8F%BD%E2%99%80%EF%B8%8F-issue-closed-"
"reasons>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:260
#: eae0a516832948c699a1a96c3552d49d
msgid ""
"Being closed as ``completed`` means that the issue has been fixed (in the "
"case of bugs) or done (in the case of enhancements and tasks). More "
"precisely, it means that a commit containing the relevant work has been "
"pushed. It takes time for this work to make its way into a package, which "
"must then go through the :doc:`testing </user/downloading-installing-"
"upgrading/testing>` process before finally landing in the relevant stable "
"repository. Automated comments on the issue will announce when key events in "
"this process occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:262
#: b151d52f354740a59c93ef1da25bc3c2
msgid ""
"Being closed as ``not planned`` means that the issue will *not* be fixed (in "
"the case of bugs) or done (in the case of enhancements and tasks). When an "
"issue is closed as ``not planned``, we add a **resolution** label starting "
"with ``R:`` that specifies the reason for the closure, such as ``R: "
"duplicate`` or ``R: cannot reproduce``. Each of these labels has a "
"description that briefly explains the label. We also leave a comment "
"containing a longer explanation for why the issue is being closed along with "
"general information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:264
#: f33bf901f7214f9b8a1cda708a3798bd
msgid ""
"While issues that are closed as ``not planned`` get a more specific "
"resolution label, issues that are closed as ``completed`` do not always get "
"one, since the linked PRs, commits, automated messages, and the "
"``completed`` reason itself are often sufficient to convey all relevant "
"information. For information about using closure reasons in searches, see :"
"ref:`introduction/issue-tracking:search tips`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:267
#: a1f85bcd4fcf47f898b37ad0d7455b69
msgid "Backports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:270
#: a6e95e9843394405ab52ab17006ab80c
msgid ""
"Issues in GitHub can only be open or closed, but when it comes to bugs that "
"affect multiple versions of Qubes OS, there are several possible states:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:272
#: c86a84ea6ae7432dbcd06164c04f3900
msgid "Not fixed yet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:274
#: e3fdca85868745aeada7940038bb794c
msgid "Fix developed but not yet committed (PR open)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:276
#: 1ba8e724a88a4d94bb7bdfd6b128e79a
msgid "Fix committed (PR merged), but update not yet pushed to any repo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:278
#: ca475bb7b40748e387036952230ef64d
msgid "Update pushed to testing repo for the most recent development version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:280
#: ca672ff649d546ff973970ac0c9740cf
msgid "Update pushed to stable repo for the most recent development version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:282
#: 8de6e41b4cd44104858ebfa96fca32c0
msgid "Update backported to stable version(s) and pushed to the testing repo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:284
#: cf98081a18634a8f984f7657db9b6722
msgid "Update pushed to stable repo of stable version(s)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:288
#: 53a3d1baa9ee4a2a96ef6cac71cf79c5
msgid ""
"We close issues at step 3. Then, as updates are released, the issue "
"automatically gets the appropriate ``current-testing`` (``rX.Y-*-cur-test``) "
"and ``stable`` (``rX.Y-*-stable``) labels. Based on these labels, it’s "
"possible to select issues waiting for step 6 (see `issues by release "
"<https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues#issues-by-release>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:290
#: eda5fd21f7a14d5a84ddaf127bb9e287
msgid ""
"Therefore, if you see that an issue is closed, but the fix is not yet "
"available to you, be aware that it may be at an intermediate stage of this "
"process between issue closure and the update being available in whichever "
"repos you have enabled in whichever version of Qubes you’re using."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:292
#: 38c69ef164ec4832886ac77401cec87c
msgid ""
"In order to assist with this, we have a label called `backport pending "
"<https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/labels/backport%20pending>`__, "
"which means, “The fix has been released for the testing release but is "
"pending backport to the stable release.” Our infrastructure will attempt to "
"apply this label automatically, when appropriate, but it is not perfect, and "
"the developers may need to adjust it manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:295
#: 7593f890c937450e93a017657a51b16f
msgid "Understanding open and closed issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:298
#: 5c059af9440e475798ec1f4607efbf46
msgid ""
"Every issue is always in one of two states: open or closed, with open being "
"the default. The **open** and **closed** states mean that, according to our "
"available information at present, the issue in question either **is** or "
"**is not** (respectively) actionable for the Qubes team. The open and closed "
"states do not mean anything more than this, and it’s important not to read "
"anything else into them. It’s also important to understand that closing an "
"issue is, in effect, nothing more than changing a virtual tag on an issue. "
"Closing an issue is never “final” in any sense, and it does not affect the "
"issue itself in any other way. Issues can be opened and closed instantly "
"with a single button press an unlimited number of times at no cost. In fact, "
"since the open and closed states reflect our available information at "
"present, one should expect these states to change back and forth as new "
"information becomes available. Closed issues are fully searchable, just like "
"open issues, and we explicitly instruct all users of the issue tracker to "
"search *both* open *and* closed issues, which GitHub makes easy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:301
#: f48ba2bb528f41c8a55df0af9c0799b5
msgid "Workflow and what do issue states mean"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:304
#: 2342642e69ad4d7d9b9d45896b3ac56d
msgid "There are some rules we use when assigning issues and tagging them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:307
#: eeae7cdcb9a5416c9b4946904571c9cc
msgid "Assigning issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:310
#: d545a789baca49bc9aefcb6efc4a29e7
msgid ""
"To avoid a situation where an issue is “dead” - assigned to someone who is "
"not actively working on it - and to help the team organize their work, an "
"issue should be assigned to a person who currently works on it, or will "
"start working on it in a very near future (about a week or two). One person "
"can have several issues assigned at the same time (for example they may be "
"working on one another issue while waiting for review), but if an issue is "
"no longer actively being worked on (for example when it’s blocked by "
"something else), it should be unassigned. At that point, if there is some "
"partial work already done, there should be a comment about that, including "
"link to the code (some WIP commit in some branch?) if applicable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:312
#: ad9ed006e16f41358ef4fd18a3dd769b
msgid ""
"Issues should not be assigned as a todo-list several months in the future, "
"or assigned to someone without their explicit confirmation that they are "
"currently working on that issue or will start doing it shortly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:315
#: f91f6aefd24048868ad5397edef7b573
msgid "Working on an issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:318
#: 4bf034977a164b7fa1a9da7d09705831
msgid ""
"Every issue should involve a clear statement of success: when is the issue "
"finished? It might not be clear to the person making the issue, especially "
"if it’s an enhancement request, but before work starts, the person working "
"on the issue should make sure that it includes clear completion criteria in "
"the description (via editing the description, if necessary). The completion "
"criteria would ideally be a checklist, and consist of a list of pull "
"requests/features, each preferably no more than two weeks of work. It’s also "
"important to remember tests and documentation should also be part of the "
"issue, if applicable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:320
#: 83de838192034b5b9d3e911b9fca9af3
msgid ""
"An issue should also have a rough estimate how much time it needs, if it’s "
"more than one-two days. Of course this might be updated later, if an issue "
"turns out to be more (or maybe less) complicated than it has initially "
"seemed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/issue-tracking.rst:322
#: 5db45be65db4486ea748d282ce7bd3e1
msgid ""
"When an issue is done (that is, the completion checklist has been "
"completed), the issue should be moved to **ready** column in the *Current "
"team tasks* project."
msgstr ""
